  "editorial": "list.pop(0) moves every later element. deque.popleft does not. The popped sequence is the FIFO order, which is what you assert while the structure choice is what makes the cost constant per operation.",
  "reference_solution": "def solve(ops):\n    from collections import deque\n    queue = deque()\n    out = []\n    for op in ops:\n        if op[0] == \"enq\":\n            queue.append(op[1])\n        elif queue:\n            out.append(queue.popleft())\n    return out\n"
}
